# Electron
# Both spellings on purpose. "node_modules/" matches a directory but NOT a
# symlink of the same name, and symlinking node_modules is how you run several
# git worktrees off one install instead of paying a full install per tree.
# Without the bare form, "git add -A" commits the symlink -- which happened in
# #193 and had to be undone in #194. Do not "tidy" this back to one line.
node_modules/
node_modules
input_viewer_electron/dist/
input_viewer_electron/out/

# Test reports (CI writes these; useful locally too)
input_viewer_electron/junit.xml

